WEBVTT

00:00:58.100 --> 00:01:00.831
in the lungs, they line air sacs
for gas exchange.

00:01:00.855 --> 00:01:02.594
In muscle, they corkscrew,

00:01:02.618 --> 00:01:05.854
so that muscles can contract
without cutting off circulation.

00:01:05.878 --> 00:01:08.401
And in nerves, they course along
like power lines,

00:01:08.425 --> 00:01:09.846
keeping those nerves alive.

00:01:10.449 --> 00:01:12.480
We get most of these blood vessels

00:01:12.504 --> 00:01:14.401
when we're actually still in the womb.

00:01:14.766 --> 00:01:16.976
And what that means is that as adults,

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.247
blood vessels don't normally grow.

00:01:19.271 --> 00:01:22.000
Except in a few special circumstances.

00:01:22.787 --> 00:01:24.976
In women, blood vessels grow every month,

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.817
to build the lining of the uterus.

00:01:26.841 --> 00:01:29.268
During pregnancy, they form the placenta,

00:01:29.292 --> 00:01:31.529
which connects mom and baby.